E["npc:hansel-heavyhands"] = {t="npc",n="Hansel Heavyhands",z="searinggorge",s="Hansel Heavyhands is an unusually massive Dark Iron dwarf stationed with the Thorium Brotherhood atop Thorium Point in the Searing Gorge. Tasked with perilous field work by the outpost's overseers, he consistently delegates dangerous jobs to passing adventurers using a colorful array of petty physical complaints. His hulking frame stands out among his kin, even if his enthusiasm for fieldwork does not match his size.",h="Hansel Heavyhands is an unusually massive Dark Iron dwarf stationed with the Thorium Brotherhood atop Thorium...",sec={{t="A Giant Among Dwarves",b="Even by the broad-shouldered standards of the Dark Iron clan, Hansel Heavyhands is an anomaly. Towering over his brethren with a massive frame that borders on orcish in width and height, his sheer physical presence suggests a warrior built for frontline slaughter. Yet despite his imposing build and formidable moniker, Hansel appears utterly uninterested in unnecessary physical exertion, preferring the relative security of the Thorium Brotherhood's camp high above the volcanic ash.",sp=0},{t="Master of Excuses",b="Taskmaster Scrange and Master Smith Burninate frequently assign Hansel the grim chore of culling the fiery beasts lurking in the slag pits below. When told to clear out the predatory Incendosaurs crawling through the Cauldron, Hansel begs off citing sore feet. When ordered to exterminate the Greater Lava Spiders infesting the searing wastes, he claims the blasted volcanic ridge is afflicted with a 'frigid climate' that has given him a miserable cold. Consequently, any mercenary willing to brave the magma flows finds Hansel ready with an open contract.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hansel Heavyhands?",a="Hansel Heavyhands is a Dark Iron dwarf aligned with the Thorium Brotherhood. Stationed at Thorium Point in the Searing Gorge, he is known for his startlingly enormous physical size and his uncanny knack for dodging dangerous fieldwork.",al={"who is hansel","hansel heavyhands lore","hansel dwarf"}},{q="Why is Hansel so much bigger than other dwarves?",a="No clear explanation is given for his bulk. Hansel is simply an abnormally gigantic Dark Iron dwarf, possessing broad shoulders, thick limbs, and an overall stature approaching that of an orc.",al={"why is hansel so big","huge dwarf searing gorge","orc sized dwarf"}},{q="What tasks does Hansel give to adventurers?",a="Hansel recruits passing travelers to handle assignments handed down by his superiors. Specifically, he pays mercenaries to exterminate Greater Lava Spiders throughout the Searing Gorge and hunt Incendosaurs deep within the Cauldron.",al={"hansel heavyhands quests","what quests does hansel give"}},{q="Why doesn't Hansel do his own chores?",a="Hansel comes up with excuses whenever danger calls. He blames sore feet for keeping him out of the Cauldron to fight Incendosaurs, and he complains that the blistering Searing Gorge is freezing enough to give him a cold when ordered to hunt lava spiders.",al={"why doesnt hansel fight","hansel excuses"}},{q="Is Hansel loyal to the Dark Iron emperor?",a="Hansel belongs to the Thorium Brotherhood, a renegade faction of Dark Iron dwarves that has broken away from Emperor Dagran Thaurissan and Ragnaros. He is neutral toward both Alliance and Horde travelers visiting Thorium Point.",al={"is hansel loyal to shadowforge","is hansel an enemy"}},{q="Where can Hansel Heavyhands be found?",a="He is located at Thorium Point, the rocky outpost perched on the northern ridge overlooking the Searing Gorge.",al={"hansel location","where is hansel"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarves may marvel—or scoff—at Hansel's colossal build, wondering how a Dark Iron grew to such towering proportions while spending his days dodging actual labor.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though the Alliance generally clashes with Dark Iron loyalists, the Thorium Brotherhood welcomes anyone with a strong arm, making Hansel a convenient source of local bounty work.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde travelers will find Hansel's sheer bulk reminiscent of an orc or tauren, though his reluctance to engage in honorable combat will certainly raise an eyebrow."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","hansel heavyhands","incendosaur","lava spider","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood","thorium point"},rel={"subzone:thorium-point","zone:searinggorge","subzone:cauldron","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","topic:dwarf","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Hansel Heavyhands"}}
E["npc:velarok"] = {t="npc",n="Velarok",z="searinggorge",s="Velarok Windblade is a lone human swordsman camped amid the ash and cinder of Searing Gorge, flanked by the mutilated corpses of Dark Iron dwarves. He seeks vengeance against the local Dark Irons for the brutal murder of his father, recruiting passing travelers to forge a weapon of retribution. His single-minded hunger for vengeance drives everything he asks of those who help him.",h="Velarok Windblade is a lone human swordsman camped amid the ash and cinder of Searing Gorge, flanked by the...",sec={{t="A Son's Vengeance",b="Found southeast of Thorium Point, Velarok Windblade presents himself as a grieving human warrior stranded in the perilous wastes of the Searing Gorge. Surrounding his camp are the bloody, battered corpses of Dark Iron dwarves who crossed his blade. According to Velarok, these clan dwarves slaughtered his father in cold blood. Consumed by hatred, he enlists travelers to gather materials to assemble the Torch of Retribution, an enchanted weapon of vengeance against the Dark Irons and the minions of Ragnaros.",sp=0},{t="The Deceiver Unmasked",b="The tale of a slain father is entirely a fabrication. Once the Torch of Retribution is fully assembled and energized, the human illusion shatters, exposing the figure as Velarok the Deceiver—a cunning drake of the black dragonflight. Having manipulated mortals into undermining the Dark Iron dwarves for the brood's own designs, Velarok spares his useful pawns out of amusement, leaving behind petty trinkets through his servant before taking wing toward Blackrock Mountain.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Who is Velarok?",a="Velarok Windblade initially appears to be a vengeful human swordsman camping southeast of Thorium Point in Searing Gorge, seeking retribution against the Dark Iron clan for his father's demise.",al={"who is velarok windblade","velarok identity","velarok lore"},sp=2},{q="Why is Velarok surrounded by dead dwarves?",a="The mutilated Dark Iron remains scattered around his camp are the grim evidence of the blood feud he says he is waging against the clan for his father's death.",al={"mutilated dark iron remains","dead dwarves near velarok","velarok camp bodies"},sp=2},{q="What is the Torch of Retribution?",a="It is an enchanted torch assembled from rare materials gathered across Searing Gorge in the name of vengeance. Velarok has his helpers collect the pieces, combines and enchants them himself, and then binds the finished torch to the one who helped him.",al={"torch quest velarok","what is the torch of retribution"},sp=1},{q="Why does Velarok disguise himself as a human?",a="Disguising as a human allows him to recruit Alliance and Horde adventurers without drawing suspicion. Black dragons frequently use mortal guises to orchestrate proxy strikes against their enemies, such as the Dark Iron servants of Ragnaros.",al={"why is velarok human","why deceive players","velarok the deceiver disguise"},sp=2},{q="Where does Velarok go after revealing himself?",a="Upon revealing his true dragon form as Velarok the Deceiver, he takes flight and heads toward Blackrock Mountain to rejoin his brood, leaving his mortal servant to award the adventurers who assisted him.",al={"where did velarok fly","velarok ending","what happens to velarok"},sp=2},{q="Does Velarok attack when his disguise drops?",a="No. Velarok considers the adventurers' unwitting service amusing and satisfactory. Rather than destroying them, he spares their lives and permits them to receive minor trinkets from his servant.",al={"do i fight velarok","does velarok turn hostile"},sp=2}},ang={["race:Human"]="Velarok's tale of a murdered father and a son's vengeance plays on the ideals of filial duty and righteous retribution that many humans hold dear.",["race:Dwarf"]="Dark Iron dwarves are enemies of Ironforge, and a stranger's vow of vengeance against them may find ready sympathy among Bronzebeards, though the Searing Gorge breeds more cunning evils than the Dark Irons alone."},kw={"searing gorge","thorium point","torch of retribution","velarok","velarok windblade"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","topic:black-dragonflight","subzone:blackrock-mountain","subzone:thorium-point"},src={"Velarok"}}
E["quest:3181"] = {t="quest",n="The Horn of the Beast",z="searinggorge",s="A gigantic horn that came from Margol the Rager in Searing Gorge is scratched and cracked, with a broken axe head lodged in its rough surface. The axe head is etched as the property of Mountaineer Pebblebitty, and it shatters into a million pieces when you try to dislodge it. The horn is to be taken to Pebblebitty.",h="A gigantic horn that came from Margol the Rager in Searing Gorge is scratched and cracked, with a broken axe...",sec={{t="A Shattered Clue",b="The horn from Margol the Rager is covered in scratches and cracks. Lodged in it is an unusual metal object, a broken axe head etched to show that it belonged to Mountaineer Pebblebitty. When you try to work it free, it shatters into a million pieces.",sp=0},{t="The Gate",b="This horn starts the chain that opens Stonewrought Pass, which runs between Loch Modan and Searing Gorge. It is to be taken to Mountaineer Pebblebitty, who is not willing to open the gate.",sp=0},{t="At the Gate",b="Pebblebitty calls the horn an obvious fake. Having come face to face with Margol, Pebblebitty says her horn is far bigger, eight times the size of yours at the very least, and that yours probably came off a stormsnout in the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this horn come from?",a="It comes from Margol the Rager in Searing Gorge.",al={"where do i find the horn","margol the rager location","who drops the horn"}},{q="Who is Mountaineer Pebblebitty?",a="Pebblebitty is the mountaineer to whom the horn is to be taken, and the one who is not willing to open the gate.",al={"pebblebitty","who is pebblebitty","mountaineer pebblebitty"}},{q="What happens to the axe head in the horn?",a="It is etched as the property of Mountaineer Pebblebitty, and it shatters into a million pieces when you try to dislodge it.",al={"why was pebblebitty axe in the horn","axe head inscription"}},{q="What does the horn lead to?",a="It begins the chain that opens the way through Stonewrought Pass, linking Loch Modan and Searing Gorge.",al={"stonewrought pass","what is the key to searing gorge"},sp=1}},kw={"gigantic horn","loch modan","margol the rager","pebblebitty","searing gorge","stonewrought pass"},rel={"subzone:stonewrought-pass","zone:searinggorge","zone:lochmodan"},m={start="Margol's Gigantic Horn",["end"]="Mountaineer Pebblebitty",level="43",faction="Alliance",id=3181},src={"The Horn of the Beast"}}
E["quest:3367"] = {t="quest",n="Suntara Stones",z="searinggorge",s="Dorius Stonetender is badly hurt in Searing Gorge, light-headed, with the world spinning and bleeding inside. He says he must get back to Ironforge and begs for your help to get him there.",h="Dorius Stonetender is badly hurt in Searing Gorge, light-headed, with the world spinning and bleeding inside.",sec={{t="A Plea for Help",b="Dorius groans that he is badly injured. He feels light-headed, the world is spinning, and he is bleeding internally. His one wish is to get back to Ironforge, and he asks you to help him make the journey.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Pass",b="The road ends just short of Stonewrought Pass. There Dorius is shot and dies, and a letter he was carrying falls to the ground, singed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dorius Stonetender?",a="Dorius Stonetender is badly injured in Searing Gorge and needs help getting back to Ironforge.",al={"who is dorius","dorius stonetender","injured dwarf searing gorge"}},{q="Where is Dorius trying to go?",a="He wants to get back to Ironforge.",al={"dorius destination","where does dorius go","dorius escort location"}},{q="What condition is Dorius in?",a="He is badly injured, light-headed, and bleeding internally, with the world spinning around him.",al={"dorius condition","is dorius hurt","why does dorius need help"}}},kw={"dorius stonetender","ironforge","searing gorge","singed letter","stonewrought pass","suntara stones"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:stonewrought-pass","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Dorius Stonetender",["end"]=":Singed Letter",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=3367},src={"Suntara Stones"}}
E["quest:3368"] = {t="quest",n="Suntara Stones",z="searinggorge",s="A singed letter that Dorius let fall is written to his brother. It tells of the Suntara stones, which are real and in the hands of the Dark Irons, whose leader Lathoric the Black uses their power to enslave Dorius's excavation team. It is meant for Thorius at the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge, and you are the one to carry it there.",h="A singed letter that Dorius let fall is written to his brother.",sec={{t="The Dead Man's Letter",b="In the letter, Dorius writes to his brother that if it is being read, he is gone. The stones exist, and the Dark Irons hold them. Their leader, Lathoric the Black, uses their power to enslave Dorius's excavation team. The team was taken to the cauldron, and their minds are twisted as they toil by day and by night to finish something called Obsidion. Dorius begs his brother to help them, his final wish, and asks that those who bring the letter be thanked.",sp=0},{t="Thorius Hears the News",b="Thorius sobs as the letter is brought. Then Thorius dries his face and swears in the name of the Light that Dorius will have his wish.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wrote the singed letter?",a="Dorius wrote it to his brother, as a message to be read after his death.",al={"who wrote the letter","author of singed letter","dorius letter"}},{q="Where does Thorius reside?",a="Curator Thorius can be found in the Hall of Explorers in Ironforge.",al={"where is thorius","curator thorius location","thorius hall of explorers"}},{q="What happened to Dorius's excavation team?",a="The letter says Lathoric the Black and the Dark Irons are using the stones to enslave them. They were taken to the cauldron.",al={"what happened to the dig team","dorius excavation team","enslaved miners cauldron"}},{q="What is the enslaved team working on?",a="The letter says their minds are twisted, and they toil by day and by night on something called Obsidion.",al={"what is obsidion","cauldron excavation project","dark iron project obsidion"}},{q="Who is Lathoric the Black?",a="The letter names him as the leader of the Dark Irons, who hold the Suntara stones and use their power to enslave Dorius's team.",al={"who is lathoric","lathoric the black","dark iron leader searing gorge"}},{q="How does this follow the earlier Suntara Stones?",a="It follows the first Suntara Stones, where Dorius was shot and the letter fell from Dorius. The letter is to be carried to Ironforge.",al={"previous suntara stones quest","suntara stones chain"}}},kw={"cauldron","dorius","hall of explorers","ironforge","lathoric the black","obsidion","searing gorge","singed letter","suntara stones","thorius"},rel={"quest:3367","zone:ironforge","subzone:hall-of-explorers","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start=":Singed Letter",["end"]="Curator Thorius",level="48",faction="Alliance",id=3368},src={"Suntara Stones (2)"}}
E["quest:3372"] = {t="quest",n="Release Them",z="searinggorge",s="A dying archaeologist in Searing Gorge urges you to release those whom the power of the Suntara still drives to keep at their labor, though their bodies have given out. Everything hinges on the altar of Suntara, and a relic guarded by Twilight's Hammer must be placed upon it.",h="A dying archaeologist in Searing Gorge urges you to release those whom the power of the Suntara still drives...",sec={{t="A Dying Plea",b="Before collapsing, the archaeologist begs you to release them. Their bodies have given out, yet the Suntara's power drives them on to keep at their labor. The key, says the archaeologist, is the altar of Suntara.",sp=0},{t="The Altar of Suntara",b="Go northwest, to the hills above the cave. Idolaters of the Twilight's Hammer guard a relic there, called the Mysterious Artifact. Take it from them and bring it to the Slag Pit, to set upon the altar of Suntara.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for help with Release Them?",a="A dying archaeologist in Searing Gorge, who collapses after the plea.",al={"quest giver","who gives release them","dying archaeologist"}},{q="Where is the mysterious artifact located?",a="Twilight's Hammer Idolaters guard it in the northwest quadrant of Searing Gorge, in the hills above the cave.",al={"mysterious artifact location","where is the relic","twilight's hammer idolaters"}},{q="Where must the artifact be delivered?",a="It is carried to the Slag Pit and set on the altar of Suntara.",al={"altar of suntara location","where is the altar","where do i take the artifact"}},{q="Why are the victims unable to rest?",a="The archaeologist says the Suntara's power drives them to keep at their labor, though their bodies have given out.",al={"why release them","what is happening to them","suntara power"}}},kw={"altar of suntara","dying archaeologist","mysterious artifact","release them","searing gorge","slag pit","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:slag-pit","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Dying Archaeologist",["end"]="Altar of Suntara",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=3372},src={"Release Them"}}
E["quest:3377"] = {t="quest",n="Prayer to Elune",z="searinggorge",s="A spirit held in a cage in Searing Gorge, Zamael Lunthistle, asks if you will help him. He has not had visitors in many years, and first wants you to hear his tale.",h="A spirit held in a cage in Searing Gorge, Zamael Lunthistle, asks if you will help him.",sec={{t="A Spirit in a Cage",b="Zamael Lunthistle greets you with a praise to Elune and says that many years have passed since anyone visited him. He asks if you will help, and begins with a request that you hear his tale.",sp=0},{t="Zamael's Tale",b="Zamael was a young night elf from Darkshore when he fell in with the Twilight's Hammer, who befriended him and turned him from Elune. A vision from Elune woke him from the malaise of following the old gods, and in repentance he etched his sorrow into a tablet of pure gold as a prayer to Elune. The Twilight's Hammer found the tablet, branded him a blasphemer and had him executed, his prayer unfinished. He is now bound to the world as a spirit and held in the cage as a warning to all who would betray the Twilight's Hammer's faith. Zamael has accepted his fate, but says the prayer must be found.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zamael Lunthistle?",a="Zamael Lunthistle is a spirit held in a cage in Searing Gorge. He asks you to hear his tale.",al={"who is zamael","zamael lunthistle lore","who is the ghost in the cage"}},{q="What does Zamael ask of you?",a="He asks if you will assist him, and first that you hear his tale.",al={"what does zamael want","zamael request"}},{q="What comes after hearing Zamael's tale?",a="A second part of Prayer to Elune follows, again with Zamael.",al={"next step prayer to elune","prayer to elune chain"}}},kw={"darkshore","elune","lunthistle","prayer","repentance","searing gorge","tablet","twilight's hammer","zamael"},rel={"topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:elune","topic:night-elf","topic:old-god","zone:darkshore","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Zamael Lunthistle",["end"]="Zamael Lunthistle",level="50",faction="Alliance",id=3377},src={"Prayer to Elune (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3378"] = {t="quest",n="Prayer to Elune",z="searinggorge",s="Zamael Lunthistle asks you to find his prayer to Elune, set down on a tablet of gold. One of the idol-worshipping scoundrels must carry it, and Zamael wants it taken to Astarii Starseeker in Darnassus.",h="Zamael Lunthistle asks you to find his prayer to Elune, set down on a tablet of gold.",sec={{t="The Lost Prayer",b="Zamael's faith has been rekindled, but he says that matters little after the countless malevolent actions he has taken against the world and its inhabitants. He does not expect absolution. All he asks is that the prayer be heard, so he sends you to recover the golden tablet from the idol worshippers and carry it to Astarii Starseeker in Darnassus.",sp=0},{t="At the Temple of the Moon",b="At the Temple of the Moon, Astarii Starseeker tells you that Elune smiles upon you this evening, for a lost soul has been returned to her by your hand. Gratitude is offered for the deed.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Zamael Lunthistle?",a="Zamael Lunthistle is the one who asks you to find his prayer to Elune. His faith has been rekindled after countless malevolent actions he took against the world.",al={"zamael lunthistle lore","who gives prayer to elune","zamael"}},{q="What is the prayer inscribed on?",a="Zamael's prayer was cut into a golden tablet, and he thinks one of the idol-worshipping scoundrels carries it.",al={"prayer to elune item","golden tablet","what is the prayer"}},{q="To whom should the prayer be delivered?",a="To Astarii Starseeker in Darnassus, who is found at the Temple of the Moon.",al={"who receives prayer to elune","astarii starseeker","where do i bring the prayer"}},{q="Does Zamael expect forgiveness for his past?",a="No. He says absolution is the last thing he expects, but his prayer must be heard.",al={"does zamael want forgiveness","zamael absolution"}}},kw={"astarii starseeker","darnassus","golden tablet","prayer to elune","searing gorge","temple of the moon","zamael lunthistle"},rel={"quest:3377","subzone:temple-of-the-moon","zone:darnassus","topic:elune","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Zamael Lunthistle",["end"]="Astarii Starseeker",level="50",faction="Alliance",id=3378},src={"Prayer to Elune (2)"}}
E["quest:3441"] = {t="quest",n="Divine Retribution",z="searinggorge",s="Kalaran Windblade asks you to hear his tale in Searing Gorge. His father is dead at the hands of what lurks in the cauldron, and the Stormwind magistrate would not listen. Kalaran seeks vengeance and wants an adventurer to act for him.",h="Kalaran Windblade asks you to hear his tale in Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="A Father Slain",b="Kalaran says the filth in the cauldron killed his father. He pleaded with the Stormwind magistrate for help, but the pleas fell on deaf ears. Stormwind, he says, would rather not admit this part of the world exists, let alone send soldiers to see justice done here.",sp=0},{t="A Call for Vengeance",b="Kalaran wants vengeance, plain and simple. He stands alone apart from a lumbering oaf of a squire, and the Dark Iron dwarves, along with Ragnaros's beasts, would crush him by himself. He trusts that a brave adventurer could handle the denizens of the cauldron, and he promises riches and wealth beyond all dreams to whoever helps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kalaran Windblade?",a="Kalaran Windblade is a man in Searing Gorge whose father was slain, and who seeks vengeance. He has a squire with him.",al={"who is kalaran","kalaran story","kalaran lore"}},{q="Why is Kalaran seeking retribution?",a="Kalaran blames the filth living in the cauldron for his father's death, and he wants vengeance.",al={"why divine retribution","kalaran revenge","what happened to kalaran father"}},{q="Why didn't Stormwind help Kalaran?",a="Kalaran says the Stormwind magistrate ignored his pleas. By his account Stormwind does not wish to admit this part of the world exists, much less send soldiers to see justice done.",al={"stormwind refusal","why wont stormwind help","stormwind magistrate"}},{q="What threats does Kalaran mention?",a="He names the Dark Iron dwarves and Ragnaros's beasts, and says either would overwhelm him alone.",al={"who is in the cauldron","cauldron enemies","kalaran enemies"}},{q="What does Kalaran promise in exchange for help?",a="He promises riches and wealth beyond anyone's wildest dreams to a brave adventurer who helps him.",al={"kalaran offer","what does kalaran offer"}}},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","kalaran windblade","ragnaros","retribution","stormwind","vengeance","windblade"},rel={"subzone:cauldron","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="48",id=3441},src={"Divine Retribution"}}
E["quest:3442"] = {t="quest",n="The Flawless Flame",z="searinggorge",s="Kalaran Windblade says you made the right choice, and that the blow must fall where it does most harm: the four sentry towers. With all four aflame, an offensive can begin before anyone has time to react. To set them alight, Kalaran needs to craft the torch of flawless flame.",h="Kalaran Windblade says you made the right choice, and that the blow must fall where it does most harm: the...",sec={{t="Preparing the Torch",b="After Divine Retribution, Kalaran tells you the plan: burn the four sentry towers, so that an offensive can begin before anyone has time to react. Setting them ablaze takes the proper tool, and the tool takes materials. Kalaran will craft the torch of flawless flame if you bring four hearts of flame and four globes of golem oil, and points you first to the golems and elementals of these lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of collecting these materials?",a="Kalaran Windblade needs four hearts of flame and four globes of golem oil to make the torch that will set the four sentry towers ablaze.",al={"why collect flame and oil","purpose of flawless flame","torch of flawless flame reason"}},{q="Where do you find the required components?",a="Kalaran points you to the golems and elementals of Searing Gorge.",al={"where to find golem oil","where to find heart of flame","flawless flame materials location"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="It follows Divine Retribution, in which you heard Kalaran Windblade's tale.",al={"flawless flame prerequisite","previous quest flawless flame"}},{q="Why burn the sentry towers?",a="Kalaran says that is where the most damage can be done, and with the four towers aflame an offensive can begin before anyone has time to react.",al={"why sentry towers","sentry tower plan"}}},kw={"golem oil","heart of flame","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","sentry towers","torch of flawless flame"},rel={"quest:3441","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="48",id=3442},src={"The Flawless Flame"}}
E["quest:3443"] = {t="quest",n="Forging the Shaft",z="searinggorge",s="After The Flawless Flame, Kalaran Windblade says that holding the flawless flame takes both a shaft and a casing, and the shaft must come first. The Dark Iron slavers and taskmasters of the cauldron use enchanted thorium weapons, and eight thorium plated daggers can be reforged into a shaft.",h="After The Flawless Flame, Kalaran Windblade says that holding the flawless flame takes both a shaft and a...",sec={{t="Enchanted Alloy",b="A shaft and a casing are both needed, Kalaran says, to hold the flawless flame. The slavers and taskmasters of the Dark Irons in the cauldron fight with enchanted thorium, a metal of great sturdiness. Kalaran can break eight of their thorium plated daggers down and reforge the alloy into a shaft.",sp=0},{t="A Sharp Tongue",b="When the daggers are delivered, Kalaran has no thanks to give, only jeering. You are called an exceptional laborer and asked whether you ever thought of a different vocation: detective, junk collector, or one of those silly gnomes who comb the beaches of Azeroth with metal-detecting contraptions, hunting lost treasure.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Kalaran need thorium plated daggers?",a="Kalaran Windblade can break their alloy down and reforge it into a shaft to help hold the flawless flame.",al={"why daggers","thorium plated daggers purpose","why thorium daggers"}},{q="Who carries the required daggers?",a="Dark Iron slavers and taskmasters in the cauldron fight with weapons of enchanted thorium.",al={"who drops the daggers","where are the daggers","who has thorium daggers"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the chain?",a="It follows The Flawless Flame, in which you gathered materials for the torch of flawless flame.",al={"what quest comes before forging the shaft","quest chain position"}},{q="How many daggers are required?",a="Kalaran asks for eight thorium plated daggers.",al={"how many daggers","dagger count","how many thorium daggers"}}},kw={"cauldron","dark iron slaver","dark iron taskmaster","flawless flame","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","thorium plated dagger"},rel={"quest:3442","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="48",id=3443},src={"Forging the Shaft"}}
E["quest:3452"] = {t="quest",n="The Flame's Casing",z="searinggorge",s="After Forging the Shaft, Kalaran Windblade says one final piece is needed for the torch. A large Twilight's Hammer encampment lies to the northwest, rumored to hold symbols and idols honoring its god, and Kalaran wants a single Symbol of Ragnaros.",h="After Forging the Shaft, Kalaran Windblade says one final piece is needed for the torch.",sec={{t="A Piece for the Casing",b="Kalaran calls this the last piece the torch needs. Northwest, among the mountains, a large Twilight's Hammer encampment is rumored to hold symbols and idols honoring their god, and these could carry enough enchantment for a magical casing. Kalaran asks for one Symbol of Ragnaros and will try to draw the magic out of it. The torch of retribution lacks one thing, a suitable source of arcane energy.",sp=0},{t="The Symbol Examined",b="The symbol gives off a foul magic, which Kalaran finds ideal for the work.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is needed to create the flame's casing?",a="Kalaran Windblade asks for a single Symbol of Ragnaros, from which magic may be drawn to form the casing.",al={"flames casing item","what does kalaran need","symbol needed"}},{q="Where is the Twilight's Hammer encampment?",a="Kalaran says a large Twilight's Hammer encampment lies in the mountains to the northwest.",al={"twilights hammer location","where is the cult camp","northwest mountains cult"}},{q="Why does Kalaran want a Symbol of Ragnaros?",a="The symbols and idols of Twilight's Hammer could carry enough enchantment to form a magical casing, and Kalaran hopes to draw that magic out of one.",al={"why symbol of ragnaros","ragnaros symbol purpose","what does the symbol do"}},{q="What comes before this step in the chain?",a="It follows Forging the Shaft, in which Kalaran asked for thorium plated daggers to reforge into a shaft.",al={"previous quest","what quest before flames casing"}}},kw={"flame's casing","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","symbol of ragnaros","torch of retribution","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:3443","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="50",id=3452},src={"The Flame's Casing"}}
E["quest:3453"] = {t="quest",n="The Torch of Retribution",z="searinggorge",s="After The Flame's Casing, Kalaran Windblade asks you to wait while the pieces are joined and the torch is enchanted. The work is a channeling that must not be disturbed.",h="After The Flame's Casing, Kalaran Windblade asks you to wait while the pieces are joined and the torch is...",sec={{t="Binding the Pieces",b="With the pieces gathered, Kalaran needs a moment to join them and lay the needed enchantments on the torch. The work is a channeling that must not be interrupted, so you wait while Kalaran casts.",sp=0},{t="When the Wait Ends",b="After a while, the torch appears before Kalaran, who says it is done. Kalaran adds that there is one final matter left for you to see to.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who crafts the torch?",a="Kalaran Windblade combines the pieces and applies the enchantments, channeling magic to finish the torch.",al={"torch crafter","who makes the torch","kalaran windblade role"}},{q="What came right before this step?",a="The Flame's Casing, in which you found a Symbol of Ragnaros for Kalaran to make into the casing.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","what did i just do"}},{q="Why must you not interrupt Kalaran?",a="Kalaran is channeling, and warns you not to interrupt the process while the pieces are combined.",al={"do not interrupt","channeling process"}}},kw={"channeling","enchantment","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3452","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Kalaran Windblade",level="50",id=3453},src={"The Torch of Retribution"}}
E["quest:3454"] = {t="quest",n="The Torch of Retribution",z="searinggorge",s="With the torch made, Kalaran Windblade says it now needs an owner to be bound to, and tells you to pick it up.",h="With the torch made, Kalaran Windblade says it now needs an owner to be bound to, and tells you to pick it up.",sec={{t="Binding the Flame",b="Kalaran says the torch needs to be bound to its owner. To do that, you are told to take it up yourself.",sp=0},{t="The Torch in Hand",b="You take the torch in both hands, and hatred and anger pulse through you in waves.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who tells you to take the torch?",a="Kalaran Windblade, who says it needs to be bound to its owner.",al={"who gives the torch","torch quest giver","kalaran torch"}},{q="Why must you pick up the torch?",a="Kalaran says the torch must be bound to its owner, and tells you to take it up.",al={"why pick up the torch","torch binding"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the chain?",a="It follows the earlier Torch of Retribution step, in which you waited while Kalaran combined the pieces and enchanted them.",al={"torch quest chain","previous quest"}}},kw={"binding","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3453","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]=":Torch of Retribution",level="50",id=3454},src={"The Torch of Retribution (2)"}}
E["quest:3462"] = {t="quest",n="Squire Maltrake",z="searinggorge",s="After The Torch of Retribution, Kalaran Windblade sends you on to Squire Maltrake, an envoy of theirs. Maltrake will tell you how the torch is to be used.",h="After The Torch of Retribution, Kalaran Windblade sends you on to Squire Maltrake, an envoy of theirs.",sec={{t="A Word with the Envoy",b="Kalaran Windblade points you toward Squire Maltrake, an envoy. Maltrake is the one who will explain how the Torch of Retribution is to be used.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Squire Maltrake?",a="Kalaran Windblade, who calls Maltrake an envoy and tells you to go and hear their instructions.",al={"who gives squire maltrake","squire maltrake questgiver","who starts squire maltrake"}},{q="What is Squire Maltrake's role?",a="Maltrake is the envoy Kalaran Windblade names, and will instruct you on how the Torch of Retribution is to be used.",al={"what does squire maltrake do","who is maltrake","why talk to maltrake"}},{q="What comes before speaking to Squire Maltrake?",a="The Torch of Retribution, the step before it in the same chain.",al={"prerequisite squire maltrake","what quest comes before squire maltrake","previous quest maltrake"}}},kw={"envoy","kalaran windblade","searing gorge","squire maltrake","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3454","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Kalaran Windblade",["end"]="Squire Maltrake",level="50",id=3462},src={"Squire Maltrake (quest)"}}
E["quest:3463"] = {t="quest",n="Set Them Ablaze!",z="searinggorge",s="Squire Maltrake tells you the four towers of Searing Gorge can never be destroyed, but the Torch of Retribution can set them burning for a very long time. While they burn, no guard or sentry can hold the watch posts, and the Dark Irons lose their first line of defense.",h="Squire Maltrake tells you the four towers of Searing Gorge can never be destroyed, but the Torch of...",sec={{t="A Fire No Force Can Subdue",b="The flames the torch lights cannot be put out by any element or force. Maltrake sends you inside each of the four sentry towers, North, South, East and West, to use the torch within their walls. The Dark Irons have posted lookouts at the towers, and Maltrake warns you to beware of them.",sp=0},{t="After the Last Flame",b="Back with Maltrake after the last tower is ablaze, you hear him cry out in triumph to a master. Velarok the Deceiver answers, and he shows himself as a drake of the black dragonflight. His plan, he gloats, has worked perfectly, for you would never have helped the Blackrock legion had they simply asked. When Maltrake wonders what to do with you now, Velarok silences him: you will live to watch the Blackrock legion invade the gorge. He has Maltrake hand over trinkets, speaks of a molt, and flies off toward the gorge.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to set the towers ablaze?",a="Squire Maltrake does, and he provides the Torch of Retribution for the job.",al={"who gives set them ablaze","set them ablaze quest giver","maltrake quest"}},{q="Which towers must be ignited?",a="The four sentry towers: North, South, East and West. Each must be entered, and the torch used inside.",al={"which towers","sentry tower locations","set them ablaze towers"}},{q="Why use the Torch of Retribution instead of tearing down the towers?",a="The towers can never be destroyed. Instead, the torch sets them burning for ages, with flames no element or force can subdue.",al={"why torch","destroy sentry towers"}},{q="What was the previous step before this one?",a="Speaking with Squire Maltrake, who then gives you this undertaking.",al={"set them ablaze prerequisite","prior quest"}}},kw={"dark iron","searing gorge","sentry towers","set them ablaze","squire maltrake","torch of retribution"},rel={"quest:3462","quest:3481","zone:searinggorge","topic:black-dragonflight"},m={start="Squire Maltrake",["end"]="Squire Maltrake",level="52",id=3463},src={"Set Them Ablaze! (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3481"] = {t="quest",n="Trinkets...",z="searinggorge",s="After Set Them Ablaze!, a chest called the Hoard of the Black Dragonflight waits for you in Searing Gorge. It looks locked.",h="After Set Them Ablaze!, a chest called the Hoard of the Black Dragonflight waits for you in Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="A Locked Chest",b="The Hoard of the Black Dragonflight looks to be locked, and it is yours to open. The chest comes into being once the towers of Searing Gorge are burning.",sp=0},{t="At Your Touch",b="The chest gives way at your touch, with no key needed. Inside lies a black dragonflight molt. A passing thought wonders how much cheese could be in there, and the only way to learn is to look.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Hoard of the Black Dragonflight?",a="A chest in Searing Gorge that appears after Set Them Ablaze!. It looks to be locked.",al={"what is hoard of the black dragonflight","who owns the chest","trinkets chest location"}},{q="What comes before the chest?",a="Set Them Ablaze!, the fire-setting against the towers of Searing Gorge.",al={"trinkets prerequisite","prior quest","what leads to trinkets"}},{q="What are you asked to do with the chest?",a="Open it. The chest looks locked, but opening it is all that is asked of you.",al={"is the chest locked","how to open the chest","what to do with the chest"}}},kw={"hoard of the black dragonflight","searing gorge","set them ablaze","trinkets"},rel={"quest:3463","zone:searinggorge","topic:black-dragonflight"},m={start="Hoard of the Black Dragonflight",["end"]="Hoard of the Black Dragonflight",level="50",id=3481},src={"Trinkets..."}}
E["quest:3566"] = {t="quest",n="Rise, Obsidion!",z="searinggorge",s="After Release Them, a dying archaeologist gasps that it was all a trap, and begs you to kill the traitor for them and for Thorius. Both Lathoric the Black and Obsidion must die, and Curator Thorius in Ironforge wants proof of it.",h="After Release Them, a dying archaeologist gasps that it was all a trap, and begs you to kill the traitor for...",sec={{t="A Dying Plea",b="The archaeologist is barely able to speak. They say it was all a trap, ask for forgiveness, and plead for the traitor to be killed for them and for Thorius. Lathoric the Black and Obsidion must both fall, and Curator Thorius in Ironforge wants the head of one and the heart of the other.",sp=0},{t="A Voice Answers",b="Dorius appears and scorns you as fools. Playing on the weak feelings of his brother, he had rescuers sent so that the last Suntara stone would be taken from the Twilight's Hammer. He came across the Suntara stones at the Grimesilt Digsite, and Ragnaros's power surged through him, giving him a purpose. By Ragnaros's will Obsidion was built, to destroy the Blackrock orcs of Blackrock Spire. Reborn as an acolyte of fire, he took the name Lathoric the Black. Back in Ironforge, Thorius turns pale at the proof: his own brother set all of this up and betrayed him and Ironforge. Thorius fears the Old Gods still hold strong sway here, and that if so honorable a man could be turned so easily to Ragnaros, no one is safe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="A dying archaeologist, who begs you to avenge them and Thorius.",al={"quest giver","who starts rise obsidion","dying archaeologist"}},{q="What comes before this quest?",a="Release Them, which this follows.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite","chain before rise obsidion"}},{q="Who do you bring the proof to?",a="Curator Thorius in Ironforge, who wants proof in the form of a head and a heart.",al={"where do i return","who do i return to","where is thorius"}},{q="Who are you sent to slay?",a="Two foes: the one named Lathoric the Black, and Obsidion.",al={"who is obsidion","who is lathoric","targets"}}},kw={"curator thorius","dying archaeologist","ironforge","lathoric the black","obsidion","ragnaros","rise obsidion","searing gorge"},rel={"quest:3372","zone:searinggorge","zone:ironforge","topic:old-god"},m={start="Dying Archaeologist",["end"]="Curator Thorius",level="46",faction="Alliance",id=3566},src={"Rise, Obsidion!"}}
E["quest:4449"] = {t="quest",n="Caught!",z="searinggorge",s="Someone is locked inside a wooden outhouse in Searing Gorge, shouting for help from within. They were running from the Dark Iron dwarves, hid in there, and the geologists locked the door behind them. They want eight Dark Iron geologists taught a lesson, and fifteen pieces of silk cloth for... nothing in particular.",h="Someone is locked inside a wooden outhouse in Searing Gorge, shouting for help from within.",sec={{t="Locked In",b="The voice from the outhouse tells of fleeing the Dark Iron dwarves and ducking inside to hide. The Dark Iron geologists, with their magic, must have seen, for the door was locked on the occupant before they knew it.",sp=0},{t="Two Favors",b="The occupant wants eight Dark Iron geologists taught a lesson, and fifteen pieces of silk cloth too, though the reason for the silk trails off into stammering and ends up as nothing in particular.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is trapped inside the outhouse?",a="A person who is not named, who ran from the Dark Iron dwarves and hid in there.",al={"who is in the outhouse","who is locked in the outhouse","outhouse guy"}},{q="Why does the occupant want silk cloth?",a="They ask for fifteen pieces but stumble over the reason and claim it is for nothing.",al={"why silk cloth","what is the silk for","why does outhouse guy want silk"}},{q="Who locked the outhouse door?",a="The Dark Iron geologists. The occupant believes they saw them hide and then used their magic ways to lock the door.",al={"who locked the door","who trapped the guy","which dark iron dwarves"}},{q="How many geologists must be slain?",a="The occupant asks for eight of them to be dealt with.",al={"how many geologists","geologist count"}}},kw={"caught","dark iron geologists","searing gorge","silk cloth","wooden outhouse"},rel={"quest:4450","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wooden Outhouse",["end"]="Wooden Outhouse",level="45",id=4449},src={"Caught!"}}
E["quest:4450"] = {t="quest",n="Ledger from Tanaris",z="searinggorge",s="After Caught!, the occupant of the wooden outhouse in Searing Gorge offers you a small job taken on in Tanaris. Krinkle Goodsteel in Gadgetzan wants certain things found in the gorge and a few other places, and you are to collect them and bring them to him.",h="After Caught!, the occupant of the wooden outhouse in Searing Gorge offers you a small job taken on in...",sec={{t="A Job from Tanaris",b="Having been helped, the occupant recalls a little job taken on while in Tanaris. Krinkle Goodsteel of Gadgetzan wants a list of things gathered, some from this gorge and some from elsewhere. Goodsteel's ledger will be slid under the door for you, and you are to carry it, along with everything on it, to Goodsteel in Tanaris.",sp=0},{t="What the Ledger Lists",b="The ledger lists twenty solid crystal leg shafts, which come from the glassweb spiders of Searing Gorge, and an overdue package. The package is at a crashed zeppelin at Beezil's Wreck, in Dustwallow Marsh. The third item, Goodsteel's balanced flameberge, is held by Jarquia, a murloc along the eastern shore of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this begin?",a="At the wooden outhouse in Searing Gorge, after you have helped the person locked inside.",al={"quest start","who gives ledger from tanaris","outhouse location"}},{q="Who is Krinkle Goodsteel?",a="He is in Gadgetzan, in Tanaris. He says he is awfully busy, with many patrons asking for his services.",al={"who is krinkle goodsteel","krinkle goodsteel gadgetzan","where is krinkle goodsteel"}},{q="What is on the ledger?",a="Twenty solid crystal leg shafts, an overdue package, and Goodsteel's balanced flameberge.",al={"what items are needed","ledger item list","goodsteel ledger items"}},{q="Where is the overdue package?",a="At the crashed zeppelin at Beezil's Wreck, in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"overdue package location","where is overdue package","beezil's wreck package"}},{q="Who has Goodsteel's balanced flameberge?",a="Jarquia, a murloc along the Swamp of Sorrows' east coast.",al={"balanced flameberge location","who drops flameberge","jarquia swamp of sorrows"}},{q="What came before this?",a="Caught!, at the same wooden outhouse.",al={"previous quest","prerequisite quest","chain before ledger from tanaris"}}},kw={"beezil's wreck","dustwallow marsh","gadgetzan","glassweb spiders","jarquia","krinkle goodsteel","ledger from tanaris","searing gorge","swamp of sorrows","wooden outhouse"},rel={"quest:4449","subzone:gadgetzan","zone:tanaris","zone:searinggorge","subzone:beezil-s-wreck","zone:dustwallow","zone:swampofsorrows","topic:murloc"},m={start="Wooden Outhouse",["end"]="Krinkle Goodsteel",level="46",id=4450},src={"Ledger from Tanaris"}}
E["quest:4451"] = {t="quest",n="The Key to Freedom",z="searinggorge",s="A small brass key has found its way to you in Searing Gorge. A few words are scratched into its head, marking it as a Dark Iron outhouse key that is not to be copied. Where it leads, you cannot yet say.",h="A small brass key has found its way to you in Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="A Marked Key",b="The brass key looks simple, but for the words scratched into its head, which read Dark Iron Outhouse and warn against duplicating it. Where it leads is unknown, and the way to learn is to search Searing Gorge for a use for it.",sp=0},{t="An Interrupted Visit",b="At the wooden outhouse someone coughs and asks who it is, annoyed at being disturbed. Delighted that you found the key, the occupant, Locheed, says the Dark Irons hid it after locking him in.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is written on the Grimesilt Outhouse Key?",a="Its head is scratched with the words Dark Iron Outhouse and a warning not to duplicate it.",al={"key inscription","what does key say","outhouse key text"}},{q="Where does this key lead?",a="That is for you to find out. The key marks itself as belonging to a Dark Iron outhouse, and a use for it is to be found somewhere in Searing Gorge.",al={"where to use key","outhouse location","key to freedom turn in"}}},kw={"dark iron outhouse","grimesilt outhouse key","locheed","searing gorge","the key to freedom","wooden outhouse"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Grimesilt Outhouse Key",["end"]="Wooden Outhouse",level="47",id=4451},src={"The Key to Freedom"}}
E["quest:7701"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Overseer Maltorius",z="searinggorge",s="A bounty notice declares that Overseer Maltorius, a rogue Thorium Brotherhood agent and newly hired commander of the Dark Iron Slag Pit crew of the Cauldron, is to die. By order of Overseer Oilfist, his head must be brought back as proof to Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker.",h="A bounty notice declares that Overseer Maltorius, a rogue Thorium Brotherhood agent and newly hired commander...",sec={{t="A Price on a Traitor",b="Overseer Maltorius, a traitorous Dark Iron dwarf, is to be found in the depths of the Cauldron's Slag Pit. The order is to slay him, take his head, and carry it back to Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker for the bounty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Overseer Maltorius?",a="A traitorous Dark Iron dwarf. The notice calls him a rogue Thorium Brotherhood agent and the newly hired commander of the Dark Iron Slag Pit crew of the Cauldron.",al={"maltorius lore","who is maltorius","overseer maltorius backstory"}},{q="Where can Overseer Maltorius be found?",a="Down in the Slag Pit, which belongs to the Cauldron.",al={"maltorius location","where is maltorius","how to find overseer maltorius"}},{q="Who ordered the death of Overseer Maltorius?",a="Overseer Oilfist, who is named in the notice as having given the order.",al={"who posted the bounty","who wants maltorius dead","who ordered the kill"}},{q="Who receives proof of Maltorius's death?",a="Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker, in Searing Gorge. The head of Maltorius is the proof asked for.",al={"who to turn in maltorius head","where to bring maltorius head","lolo longstriker location"}}},kw={"bounty","cauldron","lolo longstriker","overseer maltorius","overseer oilfist","searing gorge","slag pit","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"subzone:slag-pit","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found",["end"]="Lookout Captain Lolo Longstriker",level="50",id=7701},src={"WANTED: Overseer Maltorius"}}
E["quest:7704"] = {t="quest",n="Look at the Size of It!",z="searinggorge",s="You have come into a gigantic, ornate pillow that once belonged to Chambermaid Pillaclencher. Evonice Sootsmoker, in the Searing Gorge, is bound to want it.",h="You have come into a gigantic, ornate pillow that once belonged to Chambermaid Pillaclencher.",sec={{t="A Pillow for Evonice",b="The pillow Chambermaid Pillaclencher kept is now yours. Evonice Sootsmoker will surely be eager to get hold of it. Bring it to her in the Searing Gorge and see what she offers you for the trouble.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who wants Chambermaid Pillaclencher's pillow?",a="Evonice Sootsmoker, in the Searing Gorge, expected to want it badly.",al={"who do i bring the pillow to","evonice sootsmoker pillow","where does the pillow go"}},{q="Where does this pillow come from?",a="It belonged to Chambermaid Pillaclencher, and is gigantic and ornate.",al={"pillow drop","who drops the pillow","chambermaid pillow"}},{q="Where can Evonice Sootsmoker be found?",a="In the Searing Gorge.",al={"evonice location","where is evonice sootsmoker","evonice searing gorge"}}},kw={"chambermaid pillaclencher","evonice sootsmoker","look at the size of it","pillow","searing gorge"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Chambermaid Pillaclencher's Pillow",level="50",id=7704},src={"Classic quest text: Look at the Size of It!"}}
E["quest:7722"] = {t="quest",n="What the Flux?",z="searinggorge",s="Master Smith Burninate says that when Maltorius left their clan, he took their recipe for fiery flux, worth more than a pristine arcane crystal. Burninate wants the secret plans back and is sure they are near Maltorius, deep in the Slag Pit.",h="Master Smith Burninate says that when Maltorius left their clan, he took their recipe for fiery flux, worth...",sec={{t="The Stolen Recipe",b="Master Smith Burninate calls Maltorius a traitor who left the clan with the recipe for fiery flux. Burninate would bet the recipe came with Maltorius's new promotion among the Dark Irons, and wants the secret plans returned.",sp=0},{t="Into the Slag Pit",b="Burninate is sure the plans are not far from Maltorius, down in the depths of the Slag Pit. The Secret Plans: Fiery Flux are what Burninate wants carried back.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who stole the recipe for fiery flux?",a="Maltorius, whom Master Smith Burninate calls a traitor to their clan.",al={"who stole the recipe","who took the plans","what the flux traitor"}},{q="Where are the secret plans?",a="Burninate believes they are close to Maltorius, deep in the Cauldron's Slag Pit.",al={"where are the plans","secret plans fiery flux location","where to find fiery flux plans"}},{q="Who asks for the plans to be recovered?",a="It is Burninate, a master smith, who wants them back.",al={"who gives what the flux","what the flux quest giver"}},{q="Why do the plans matter to Burninate?",a="Burninate says the recipe for fiery flux is worth more than a pristine arcane crystal, and it was the clan's own secret.",al={"why is fiery flux important","importance of fiery flux recipe"}}},kw={"burninate","cauldron","fiery flux","maltorius","plans","searing gorge","slag pit"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:cauldron","subzone:slag-pit","quest:7701"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="50",id=7722},src={"What the Flux?"}}
E["quest:7723"] = {t="quest",n="Curse These Fat Fingers",z="searinggorge",s="Hansel Heavyhands, in the Searing Gorge, can no longer dish out beatings as before, thanks to swollen fingers. Hansel asks you to go pound the heavy war golems for them.",h="Hansel Heavyhands, in the Searing Gorge, can no longer dish out beatings as before, thanks to swollen fingers.",sec={{t="Fingers Like Sausages",b="Hansel Heavyhands says the climate in the Gorge, with its thin air, makes Hansel's fingers swell until they resemble huge Thelsamar blood sausages. As a result, Hansel cannot deliver beatings the way Hansel used to, and needs you to see to Hansel's business instead.",sp=0},{t="First on the List",b="First on Hansel's agenda are the heavy war golems of the Gorge, which Hansel wants pounded hard. Twenty of them are to be destroyed. They roam the areas around the Cauldron, and you return to Hansel once enough have fallen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hansel Heavyhands?",a="Someone in the Searing Gorge whose swollen fingers keep them from fighting, so they ask you to do the pounding.",al={"hansel heavyhands","who gives curse these fat fingers","who is the quest giver"}},{q="Why can Hansel not fight the golems personally?",a="Hansel blames the climate and the thin air of the Gorge for swelling their fingers, which they liken to huge Thelsamar blood sausages.",al={"why are hansels fingers fat","fat fingers lore","hansel swollen hands"}},{q="What foes must be dealt with?",a="Twenty heavy war golems.",al={"what enemies do i fight","what does hansel want dead"}},{q="Where are the heavy war golems located?",a="They roam the areas around the Cauldron, in the Searing Gorge.",al={"where are the golems","heavy war golem location"}}},kw={"cauldron","fat fingers","hansel heavyhands","heavy war golems","searing gorge","thelsamar blood sausages"},rel={"npc:hansel-heavyhands","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Hansel Heavyhands",["end"]="Hansel Heavyhands",level="49",id=7723},src={"Classic quest text: Curse These Fat Fingers"}}
E["quest:7724"] = {t="quest",n="Fiery Menace!",z="searinggorge",s="Hansel Heavyhands says that every time he wants a moment to relax and reflect on his life, the powers that be hand him another job. Greater lava spiders are causing a ruckus in the Searing Gorge, and he wants you to kill twenty of them.",h="Hansel Heavyhands says that every time he wants a moment to relax and reflect on his life, the powers that be...",sec={{t="Another Job for Hansel",b="Hansel Heavyhands complains that the powers that be never leave him in peace. Greater lava spiders are causing a ruckus, and he would rather you did the killing than him.",sp=0},{t="The Greater Lava Spiders",b="Oilfist says the spiders shoot fire out of an awkward place, which upsets the children. Hansel wants twenty greater lava spiders slain, and they are found on the plateaus and by the lava pools of the Searing Gorge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you after the spiders?",a="Hansel Heavyhands in the Searing Gorge, who had hoped for a quiet moment and been handed another job.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","hansel"}},{q="Why do the spiders need to be killed?",a="Greater lava spiders are causing a ruckus, and Oilfist says the way they shoot fire upsets the children.",al={"why kill spiders","what did spiders do","spider problem"}},{q="Who told Hansel about the spiders?",a="Oilfist, who says the spiders shoot fire from an awkward place.",al={"who complained about spiders","oilfist"}},{q="How many greater lava spiders must be killed?",a="Hansel asks for twenty to be put down.",al={"how many spiders","spider count"}}},kw={"fiery menace","greater lava spiders","hansel heavyhands","oilfist","searing gorge","spiders"},rel={"npc:hansel-heavyhands","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Hansel Heavyhands",["end"]="Hansel Heavyhands",level="49",id=7724},src={"Fiery Menace!"}}
E["quest:7727"] = {t="quest",n="Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It",z="searinggorge",s="Hansel Heavyhands says his bunions have bunions, and he cannot do any killing with his feet in such disarray. Scrange and Burninate told him to clear out the incendosaurs of the Slag Pit, so he sends you instead to slay twenty.",h="Hansel Heavyhands says his bunions have bunions, and he cannot do any killing with his feet in such disarray.",sec={{t="Bunions upon Bunions",b="Hansel Heavyhands is in no state to fight. Scrange and Burninate told him to kill the incendosaurs so that expeditionary teams can go down into the lava pools of the Slag Pit and explore. Hansel passes the work on to you.",sp=0},{t="The Lava Pools",b="The incendosaurs occupy the lava pools down in the Slag Pit, within the Cauldron. Hansel wants twenty slain, and does not want to see you back until you have done it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hansel Heavyhands?",a="He is the one who gives you this job in the Searing Gorge. Scrange and Burninate told him to deal with the incendosaurs, but he cannot with his bunions.",al={"hansel heavyhands","who is the quest giver","who gives this quest"}},{q="Why do the incendosaurs need to be cleared out?",a="Scrange and Burninate want expeditionary teams to explore the lava pools of the Slag Pit. Incendosaurs there are said to be causing all kinds of problems.",al={"why kill incendosaurs","incendosaur purpose","why clear the slag pit"}},{q="Where are the incendosaurs found?",a="Down in the lava pools of the Slag Pit, within the Cauldron.",al={"incendosaur location","where is the slag pit","where are the lava pools"}},{q="Why won't Hansel hunt them himself?",a="His bunions have bunions, he says, and his feet are in too much disarray for any killing.",al={"why won't hansel fight","hansel's feet","hansel bunions"}}},kw={"burninate","cauldron","hansel heavyhands","incendosaur","scrange","searing gorge","slag pit"},rel={"npc:hansel-heavyhands","subzone:slag-pit","subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Hansel Heavyhands",["end"]="Hansel Heavyhands",level="49",faction="Neutral",id=7727},src={"Incendosaurs? Whateverosaur is More Like It"}}
E["quest:7728"] = {t="quest",n="STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass",z="searinggorge",s="A notice lists two items stolen: a Dark Iron tuyere and a Lookout's Spyglass. The Thorium Brotherhood is certain unscrupulous, jealous Dark Iron dwarves of the Searing Gorge took them, and whoever finds them is to take them to Taskmaster Scrange for payment.",h="A notice lists two items stolen: a Dark Iron tuyere and a Lookout's Spyglass.",sec={{t="Stolen Goods",b="The notice calls the spyglass a fine tool for lookouts and the tuyere a smithing tool that cannot be replaced. All that is known is that Dark Iron dwarves definitely took them. Whoever finds them is to return them to Taskmaster Scrange.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who posted the notice?",a="The notice speaks of the Thorium Brotherhood, who are certain that Dark Iron dwarves took the items.",al={"who wants the stolen items","who gave this quest","stolen smithing tuyere quest giver"}},{q="Who stole the tools?",a="The Thorium Brotherhood is certain it was unscrupulous and jealous Dark Iron dwarves of the Searing Gorge.",al={"who took the tuyere","who stole the spyglass","who has the stolen items"}},{q="Who receives the recovered items?",a="Taskmaster Scrange in the Searing Gorge.",al={"where do i turn this in","who is taskmaster scrange","who gets the spyglass"}},{q="What are the stolen items for?",a="The tuyere is a smithing tool that cannot be replaced, and the spyglass is a valuable monitoring tool for lookouts.",al={"what is a smithing tuyere","why does the brotherhood want the tuyere","what does the spyglass do"}}},kw={"dark iron","scrange","searing gorge","smithing","spyglass","thorium brotherhood","tuyere"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found",["end"]="Taskmaster Scrange",level="48",id=7728},src={"STOLEN: Smithing Tuyere and Lookout's Spyglass"}}
E["quest:7729"] = {t="quest",n="JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition",z="searinggorge",s="A notice announces that Taskmaster Scrange wants some capable hands to cull the competition in the Searing Gorge. The work is slaying Dark Iron Taskmasters and Dark Iron Slavers until your clothes are bloody enough, then returning to Scrange.",h="A notice announces that Taskmaster Scrange wants some capable hands to cull the competition in the Searing...",sec={{t="An Open Position",b="Scrange wants applicants to head out through the gorge and slaughter the Dark Iron Taskmasters and Dark Iron Slavers they meet: fifteen of each. Come back when your clothes are bloody enough. You will know when that is, and you are not to ask.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is offering this job?",a="Taskmaster Scrange in the Searing Gorge, who wants help culling the competition.",al={"who offers this quest","who wants the taskmasters killed","who is taskmaster scrange"}},{q="Which enemies must be slain?",a="Fifteen Dark Iron Taskmasters and fifteen Dark Iron Slavers.",al={"what do i kill","targets for job opportunity","who are the competition"}},{q="How does Scrange tell the work is done?",a="By the state of your clothes. Scrange will weigh you with and without them to be sure.",al={"how to prove kills","bloody clothes requirement","how does scrange check"}}},kw={"culling the competition","dark iron slaver","dark iron taskmaster","job opportunity","searing gorge","taskmaster scrange"},rel={"zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Wanted/Missing/Lost & Found",["end"]="Taskmaster Scrange",level="48",faction="Neutral",id=7729},src={"JOB OPPORTUNITY: Culling the Competition"}}
E["quest:7736"] = {t="quest",n="Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Kingsblood",z="searinggorge",s="After What the Flux?, Master Smith Burninate turns to replenishing the dwindling supply of fiery flux in the Searing Gorge. Burninate wants incendosaur scales, Kingsblood, and coal, and will take all you can offer.",h="After What the Flux?, Master Smith Burninate turns to replenishing the dwindling supply of fiery flux in the...",sec={{t="Fiery Flux Wanted",b="Master Smith Burninate has no time for idle talk. Fiery flux is running low, and Burninate asks for incendosaur scales, Kingsblood, and coal: two scales, four Kingsblood, and coal. Burninate will take all that you can offer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for these goods?",a="Master Smith Burninate in the Searing Gorge, who receives the goods in person.",al={"who gives this quest","burninate fiery flux","where to turn in"}},{q="What materials does Burninate want?",a="Two incendosaur scales, four Kingsblood, and some coal.",al={"what items do i need","materials for fiery flux","burninate turn in items"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="The step called What the Flux?, which Burninate gave you before this.",al={"prereq for this quest","previous quest fiery flux","what the flux prerequisite"}},{q="Why does Burninate want these goods?",a="Burninate says the supply of fiery flux is dwindling and wants it replenished.",al={"why fiery flux","burninate motivation"}}},kw={"burninate","coal","fiery flux","incendosaur","kingsblood","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"quest:7722","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="60",id=7736},src={"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Kingsblood"}}
E["quest:8241"] = {t="quest",n="Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Iron",z="searinggorge",s="After What the Flux?, Master Smith Burninate turns to replenishing the dwindling supply of fiery flux in the Searing Gorge. Burninate wants incendosaur scales, iron bars, and coal, and will take all you can offer.",h="After What the Flux?, Master Smith Burninate turns to replenishing the dwindling supply of fiery flux in the...",sec={{t="Fiery Flux Wanted",b="Master Smith Burninate has no time for idle talk. Fiery flux is running low, and Burninate asks for incendosaur scales, iron bars, and coal: two scales, four iron bars, and coal. Burninate will take all that you can offer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for these goods?",a="Master Smith Burninate in the Searing Gorge, who receives the goods in person.",al={"who gives this quest","burninate fiery flux","where to turn in"}},{q="What materials does Burninate want?",a="Two incendosaur scales, four iron bars, and some coal.",al={"what items do i need","materials for fiery flux","burninate turn in items"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="The step called What the Flux?, which Burninate gave you before this.",al={"prereq for this quest","previous quest fiery flux","what the flux prerequisite"}},{q="Why does Burninate want these goods?",a="Burninate says the supply of fiery flux is dwindling and wants it replenished.",al={"why fiery flux","burninate motivation"}}},kw={"coal","fiery flux","incendosaur scale","iron bar","master smith burninate","restoring fiery flux supplies via iron","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"quest:7722","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="60",id=8241},src={"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Iron"}}
E["quest:8242"] = {t="quest",n="Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Heavy Leather",z="searinggorge",s="After What the Flux?, Master Smith Burninate turns to replenishing the dwindling supply of fiery flux in the Searing Gorge. Burninate wants incendosaur scales, heavy leather, and coal, and will take all you can offer.",h="After What the Flux?, Master Smith Burninate turns to replenishing the dwindling supply of fiery flux in the...",sec={{t="Fiery Flux Wanted",b="Master Smith Burninate has no time for idle talk. Fiery flux is running low, and Burninate asks for incendosaur scales, heavy leather, and coal: two scales, ten pieces of heavy leather, and coal. Burninate will take all that you can offer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for these goods?",a="Master Smith Burninate in the Searing Gorge, who receives the goods in person.",al={"who gives this quest","burninate fiery flux","where to turn in"}},{q="What materials does Burninate want?",a="Two incendosaur scales, ten pieces of heavy leather, and some coal.",al={"what items do i need","materials for fiery flux","burninate turn in items"}},{q="What came before this request?",a="The step called What the Flux?, which Burninate gave you before this.",al={"prereq for this quest","previous quest fiery flux","what the flux prerequisite"}},{q="Why does Burninate want these goods?",a="Burninate says the supply of fiery flux is dwindling and wants it replenished.",al={"why fiery flux","burninate motivation"}}},kw={"burninate","coal","fiery flux","heavy leather","incendosaur scale","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood"},rel={"quest:7722","zone:searinggorge"},m={start="Master Smith Burninate",["end"]="Master Smith Burninate",level="60",id=8242},src={"Restoring Fiery Flux Supplies via Heavy Leather"}}
E["subzone:blackchar-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackchar Cave",z="searinggorge",s="Blackchar Cave is a mysterious, sealed-off cavern tucked into the southwestern crags of Searing Gorge, close to the base of Blackrock Mountain. Its entrance is choked with impassable rubble and rock.",h="Blackchar Cave is a mysterious, sealed-off cavern tucked into the southwestern crags of Searing Gorge, close...",sec={{t="A Sealed Threshold",b="Tucked away against the scorching crags near the approaches to Blackrock Mountain, Blackchar Cave presents a solid wall of stone where a deep cavern entrance might once have been. Heavy rubble and scorched slag choke the opening, preventing anyone from exploring whatever tunnels lie deeper within the mountain roots. The desolate terrain around it is scorched by ash and magma, offering little comfort to wanderers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Can you go inside Blackchar Cave?",a="No. The entrance to Blackchar Cave is completely sealed off by collapsed rock, ash, and rubble. There is no open interior space to explore.",al={"is blackchar cave open","enter blackchar cave","inside blackchar cave"}},{q="Where is Blackchar Cave located?",a="It is located in the southwestern corner of Searing Gorge, situated along the rocky foothills near the passage toward Blackrock Mountain.",al={"blackchar cave location","where is blackchar cave"}}},kw={"blackchar cave","blackrock mountain","sealed cave","searing gorge"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:blackrock-mountain"},src={"Blackchar Cave"}}
E["subzone:cauldron"] = {t="subzone",n="Cauldron",z="searinggorge",s="The Cauldron is a massive open-pit excavation site dominating the center of the Searing Gorge. Operated by the Dark Iron clan, this fiery quarry is worked day and night by broken slaves under the watch of cruel overseers and roving elementals.",h="The Cauldron is a massive open-pit excavation site dominating the center of the Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="The Molten Quarry",b="Carved deep into the scorched earth of the Searing Gorge, the Cauldron was fortified following the catastrophic summoning of Ragnaros by Emperor Thaurissan. Massive, smoke-belching Dark Iron excavation machinery rims the canyon walls, scraping rock and ore from the smoldering stone. Down within its burning crevices, living fire and magma elementals prowl alongside Dark Iron taskmasters, while subterranean heat rises continuously from the depths of the mountain.",sp=0},{t="The Broken Workforce",b="Deep within the pit, captured slave workers endure brutal, endless shifts under the lash of Dark Iron overseers. Broken by relentless labor, sweltering heat, and torment, many of these laborers have been driven completely mad. They no longer recognize friend from foe, lashing out violently against any outsiders who disturb their toil—even those who might otherwise offer them a chance at liberation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Cauldron?",a="The Cauldron is an enormous strip mine and excavation quarry located in the center of the Searing Gorge. Built and fortified by the Dark Iron clan, it serves as an industrial hub for extracting stone and ore under intensely volatile volcanic conditions.",al={"the cauldron lore","what is the cauldron","searing gorge quarry"}},{q="Who controls the excavation?",a="The Dark Iron clan controls the entire site. They oversee operations using heavy excavators and armed overseers, maintaining a brutal hold over the pit and its laborers.",al={"who runs the cauldron","cauldron masters"}},{q="Why do the slaves attack adventurers who try to help?",a="The slaves have been broken by cruel torment, blinding heat, and relentless exhaustion. Driven mad by their masters and their grueling existence, their fractured minds view any interruption to their work as a threat, causing them to attack anyone nearby.",al={"why are slaves hostile","slave workers attacking","can you free the slaves"}},{q="What kinds of creatures live inside the pit?",a="Aside from Dark Iron overseers and their enslaved workforce, the fiery fissures of the Cauldron crawl with volatile fire and magma elementals unleashed by the volcanic nature of the gorge.",al={"cauldron mobs","what is in the cauldron","monsters in cauldron"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The massive mechanical dredges and open-pit terracing of the Cauldron showcase the industrial scale of Dark Iron excavation, carved directly into volatile volcanic crust.",["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing the depravity of the Dark Irons firsthand—using sentient captives as expendable, broken labor amid fire elementals—stirs deep disgust in Ironforge dwarves."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","excavation","magma elementals","quarry","searing gorge","slave workers","slaves"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","topic:dark-iron-clan","subzone:ruins-of-thaurissan"},src={"Cauldron"}}
E["subzone:dustfire-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustfire Valley",z="searinggorge",s="Dustfire Valley is a dry, windswept gulch nestled along the northern edge of the Searing Gorge. It serves as the scorched threshold leading directly to the fortified gate of Stonewrought Pass, which bars the mountain route into Loch Modan.",h="Dustfire Valley is a dry, windswept gulch nestled along the northern edge of the Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="The Northern Boundary",b="Tucked away in northern Searing Gorge, Dustfire Valley is defined by choking ash, brittle rock, and barren canyon walls. Its most notable feature is the imposing, locked dwarven gateway sealing Stonewrought Pass. Because of these locked iron doors, direct travel north into the Valley of Kings and Loch Modan remains entirely barred to ordinary wanderers, leaving the valley an isolated cul-de-sac amidst the sulfurous wastes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the gate in Dustfire Valley lead?",a="The gate seals Stonewrought Pass, a mountain passage carved through the heights into the Valley of Kings in Loch Modan.",al={"dustfire gate","locked door dustfire","where does stonewrought pass lead"}},{q="Can you open the gate to Loch Modan?",a="The gate is locked tight by dwarven craftsmanship to protect the lands of Loch Modan from the threats of Searing Gorge. Passing through requires securing a specific key.",al={"how to open gate","open stonewrought pass","key to dustfire gate"}},{q="Why is this area called Dustfire Valley?",a="The name reflects the choking combination of volcanic ash, dry dust, and lingering heat that characterizes this canyon near the northern mountain walls.",al={"dustfire valley name","why dustfire"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, the gated passage here marks a heavily fortified back door between the safety of Khaz Modan and the treacherous territory ruled by the Dark Iron clan."},kw={"dustfire valley","loch modan","locked gate","searing gorge","stonewrought pass","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:stonewrought-pass","subzone:valley-of-kings","zone:searinggorge","zone:lochmodan"},src={"Dustfire Valley"}}
E["subzone:firewatch-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Firewatch Ridge",z="searinggorge",s="Firewatch Ridge is a high volcanic bluff in the northern reaches of Searing Gorge, serving as a primary encampment for the Dark Iron dwarves. Looming directly above the vast excavation known as the Cauldron, the ridge is heavily fortified by dwarven sentries, mechanical golems, and nesting fire spiders. To the northwest, an ominous cave system reveals an entrenched presence of the Twilight's Hammer cult.",h="Firewatch Ridge is a high volcanic bluff in the northern reaches of Searing Gorge, serving as a primary...",sec={{t="A Scorched Vantage Point",b="Perched above the industrial devastation of the Cauldron, Firewatch Ridge functions as a critical staging ground for the Dark Iron clan's operations in Searing Gorge. Dwarven guards, engineers, and molten golem creations patrol the crags, fiercely defending their foothold alongside venomous flame spiders native to the smoldering rocks. Its elevation provides the Dark Irons an unobstructed view of the surrounding ash plains, ensuring early warning against rival incursions from Ironforge or the Thorium Brotherhood.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Cult",b="Tucked away in the northwestern reaches of the ridge lies an underground cave network claimed by the Twilight's Hammer. These cultists operate in the shadows of the Dark Iron encampment, conducting dark rituals and harboring powerful elite zealots beneath the rock. Their proximity to both the Dark Iron infrastructure and Blackrock Mountain reflects the pervasive, insidious reach of elemental and apocalyptic cults within the fiery heart of the Searing Gorge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Firewatch Ridge?",a="Firewatch Ridge is an elevated ridge in Searing Gorge where the Dark Iron dwarves have established a major camp overlooking the Cauldron excavation site.",al={"what is this place","firewatch ridge info","firewatch ridge overview"}},{q="What enemies inhabit Firewatch Ridge?",a="The ridge is populated by hostile Dark Iron dwarves, mechanical golems, and native fire spiders, while the cave system to the northwest is occupied by elite members of the Twilight's Hammer cult.",al={"what mobs are here","enemies firewatch","firewatch ridge threats"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cult has entrenched itself in the northwestern caves of the ridge to pursue their elemental worship and apocalyptic rituals in close proximity to Blackrock Mountain and the fire elementals bound within the region.",al={"twilights hammer firewatch","cultists in cave","northwest cave firewatch"}},{q="How does Firewatch Ridge relate to the Cauldron?",a="Firewatch Ridge sits directly above the Cauldron, offering the Dark Iron dwarves a fortified vantage point to supervise mining operations and defend against potential strikes on their quarry.",al={"firewatch and cauldron","cauldron overlook","why overlook cauldron"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, Firewatch Ridge is a grim reminder of their Dark Iron cousins' entrenched malice, iron industry, and dark alliances in the shadow of Blackrock Mountain."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","firewatch ridge","flame spiders","golems","searing gorge","twilight's hammer"},rel={"subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Firewatch Ridge"}}
E["subzone:grimesilt-dig-site"] = {t="subzone",n="Grimesilt Dig Site",z="searinggorge",s="Grimesilt Dig Site is an archaeological excavation in the Searing Gorge originally broken ground by Ironforge dwarves. Overrun by hostile Dark Iron dwarves, the pit is now firmly under enemy control while surviving members of the original expedition struggle to endure in hiding.",h="Grimesilt Dig Site is an archaeological excavation in the Searing Gorge originally broken ground by Ironforge...",sec={{t="A Contested Excavation",b="Situated within the soot-choked badlands of the Searing Gorge, the Grimesilt Dig Site began as an expedition sanctioned by Ironforge scholars seeking relics beneath the crags. That venture met a violent end when the native Dark Iron dwarves drove out the excavators and claimed the equipment for themselves. Today, the trench swarms with Dark Iron sentries, leaving the wounded and scattered survivors of the original Ironforge crew trapped in and around the pit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who originally established the Grimesilt Dig Site?",a="The excavation was begun by the Bronzebeard dwarves of Ironforge. Their team was dispatched to unearth ancient artifacts beneath the Searing Gorge before being ambushed and displaced.",al={"who dug grimesilt","who made grimesilt dig site","grimesilt founders"}},{q="Who controls the dig site now?",a="The Dark Iron clan seized the excavation. They currently occupy the pits, guarding the remaining tools and territory against any attempts by Ironforge to reclaim the area.",al={"who owns grimesilt","grimesilt enemies","who is at grimesilt"}},{q="Are there any survivors from the original crew?",a="Yes. A few workers managed to stay alive, including the injured excavator Dorius Stonetender lying near the pit floor, and another unfortunate crewmate hiding inside a nearby outhouse.",al={"survivors at grimesilt","dorius stonetender","who is trapped at grimesilt"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard dwarves, Grimesilt is a bitter reminder of the Dark Iron threat lingering right across the mountains, underscoring the dangers facing dwarven antiquities and archaeologists in hostile lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="The dig site represents an Ironforge endeavor ruthlessly broken by the Dark Irons, leaving beleaguered Alliance subjects awaiting extraction in treacherous territory."},kw={"archaeology","dark iron","dorius stonetender","excavation","grimesilt dig site","ironforge","searing gorge"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","zone:ironforge","topic:dwarf"},src={"Grimesilt Dig Site"}}
E["subzone:sea-of-cinders"] = {t="subzone",n="Sea of Cinders",z="searinggorge",s="The Sea of Cinders is an expanse of scorched, windblown terrain lying across the southern stretch of the Searing Gorge, directly north of Blackrock Mountain. Ravaged by elemental heat and relentless gusts, the flat ground constantly vents ash and embers, creating a choking wasteland where very little can endure.",h="The Sea of Cinders is an expanse of scorched, windblown terrain lying across the southern stretch of the...",sec={{t="A Wasteland of Embers",b="Stretching between the rocky cliffs of the Searing Gorge and the imposing bulk of Blackrock Mountain, the Sea of Cinders earns its name from the suffocating haze of particulate and burning grit that constantly sweeps its plains. When the Firelord Ragnaros was summoned into the mortal world centuries ago, the violent upheaval fractured the Redridge Mountains and transformed the surrounding landscape into an arid slag heap. The Sea of Cinders is among the most barren remnants of that cataclysm, an uninhabitable plain where the earth itself refuses to cool.",sp=0},{t="Peril Beneath the Slopes",b="Because it borders the north approach to Blackrock Mountain, travelers and scavengers often have no choice but to cross these scorching flats. The winds here kick up dense clouds of blinding ash that hide sudden fissures, elemental horrors, and wandering predators adapted to the searing heat. Between the hostile environment and the looming presence of the Dark Iron dwarves who claim the region, any trek across the cinders demands vigilance and swift passage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sea of Cinders?",a="It is a desolate, ash-covered flatland located in southern Searing Gorge, right against the northern face of Blackrock Mountain. It is blanketed in smoldering dirt and flying embers.",al={"what is sea of cinders","sea of cinders lore","where is sea of cinders"}},{q="Why is the ground constantly burning?",a="The region was utterly devastated centuries ago when Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan summoned the Firelord Ragnaros during the War of the Three Hammers. The catastrophic eruption superheated the earth and shattered the mountains, leaving plains that still smolder to this day.",al={"why is it on fire","why are there cinders","why does the ground smoke"}},{q="Does anyone live here?",a="No organized settlement exists within the Sea of Cinders itself. The suffocating heat, poor air, and lack of water make permanent habitation impossible, leaving the expanse occupied only by wandering beasts, fire elementals, and patrols affiliated with Blackrock Mountain.",al={"who lives here","sea of cinders inhabitants","settlements"}},{q="What makes traveling through here dangerous?",a="Aside from the hostile fauna and Dark Iron dwarves lurking near the mountain, the environment itself is lethal. The air is thick with blinding soot and burning ash, and deep thermal rifts riddle the flat terrain.",al={"is it safe","dangers of sea of cinders"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The volatile, heat-cracked stone skirting Blackrock Mountain frequently exposes rich mineral deposits and dark iron veins to those brave enough to prospect among the drifting ash.",["race:Dwarf"]="For Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarves, walking through these burning wastes is a grim reminder of Thaurissan's folly and the dark powers that shattered the Redridge Mountains."},kw={"ash","blackrock mountain","dark iron","embers","ragnaros","sea of cinders","searing gorge","wasteland"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:blackrock-mountain"},src={"Sea of Cinders"}}
E["subzone:slag-pit"] = {t="subzone",n="Slag Pit",z="searinggorge",s="The Slag Pit is an extensive subterranean mining excavation nestled inside the Cauldron of Searing Gorge. Overseen by ruthless Dark Iron taskmasters and slavers, these fiery tunnels are driven by forced labor under the shadow of Blackrock Mountain. Trespassers must contend not only with hostile dwarf overseers, but also ravenous incendosaurs prowling the lower levels.",h="The Slag Pit is an extensive subterranean mining excavation nestled inside the Cauldron of Searing Gorge.",sec={{t="Subterranean Toil",b="Carved into the depths of the Cauldron, the Slag Pit represents the grinding industrial engine of the Dark Iron dwarves in Searing Gorge. Day and night, enslaved workers are driven to extract rich ores and minerals under the lash of brutal overseers and taskmasters. The environment is harsh and suffocating, dominated by scorching heat, choking dust, and the clatter of iron picks. The Dark Irons maintain ruthless discipline over their excavation, violently repelling any outside interference with their supply lines to Blackrock Depths.",sp=0},{t="Depths of the Pit",b="Beyond the cruelty of the slavers, the physical tunnels themselves pose a deadly hazard to workers and intruders alike. In the lower reaches of the excavation, the earth breaks open into scorching caverns inhabited by incendosaurs—ferocious reptilian beasts native to the fiery underground. Despite the constant danger of being devoured by these subterranean predators, the Dark Iron masters continue to push their labor force deeper into the rock, entirely indifferent to the lives lost in the process.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Slag Pit located?",a="The Slag Pit is located deep within the Cauldron, the massive excavation crater dominating the center of Searing Gorge. Its tunnels branch directly beneath the surface mining works.",al={"slag pit location","where is slag pit","how to get to slag pit"}},{q="Who controls the Slag Pit?",a="The mine is entirely operated by the Dark Iron clan. Dark Iron slavers and taskmasters patrol the shafts, enforcing brutal discipline and driving their captives to dig around the clock.",al={"who runs slag pit","slag pit faction","dark irons slag pit"}},{q="Why do the slave workers attack intruders?",a="While the enslaved workers are not naturally aggressive toward outsiders, their fear of their Dark Iron masters runs deep. If a slaver or taskmaster is attacked nearby, the panicked laborers will rush to their overseer's defense to avoid severe punishment.",al={"why do slaves attack","hostile slaves","slave workers aggro"}},{q="What creatures live in the Slag Pit?",a="In addition to the Dark Iron dwarves and their slaves, the deepest reaches of the pit are infested with incendosaurs—aggressive, flame-scaled saurian predators that stalk the underground tunnels.",al={"monsters in slag pit","incendosaurs","slag pit beasts"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="The deep shafts of the Slag Pit cut straight into the mineral-rich belly of Searing Gorge, making it a lucrative—if exceptionally dangerous—source of high-grade ores.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, witnessing the cruelty of the Dark Iron slavers in the Slag Pit serves as a stark reminder of the bitter divide between the clans."},kw={"cauldron","dark iron","incendosaur","searing gorge","slag pit","slaver","slaves","taskmaster"},rel={"subzone:cauldron","zone:searinggorge"},src={"Slag Pit"}}
E["subzone:stonewrought-pass"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewrought Pass",z="searinggorge",s="Stonewrought Pass is an underground tunnel cut directly through the southern mountains of Loch Modan into the blighted expanse of the Searing Gorge. Masterfully engineered by the famed architect Franclorn Forgewright, this passage connects the Valley of Kings directly to Dustfire Valley. Heavy iron gates secure both ends to protect peaceful dwarven lands from the volcanic terrors to the south.",h="Stonewrought Pass is an underground tunnel cut directly through the southern mountains of Loch Modan into the...",sec={{t="A Gateway Carved in Stone",b="Carved out of the bedrock by the legendary master architect Franclorn Forgewright—famed also for the massive Stonewrought Dam—the Stonewrought Pass serves as a direct corridor between the pastoral beauty of Loch Modan and the scorched wastes of Searing Gorge. Emerging in Loch Modan near the colossal Valley of Kings, it cuts straight through the mountain ridge down into Dustfire Valley. Because Searing Gorge is infested with Dark Iron dwarves and fiery beasts, the Ironforge mountaineers keep the passage locked tight behind heavy gates to prevent danger from spilling into the north.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Stonewrought Pass lead?",a="The pass cuts directly through the mountain range, connecting the Valley of Kings on the southern edge of Loch Modan to Dustfire Valley within the northern reaches of Searing Gorge.",al={"where does stonewrought pass go","tunnel connection","searing gorge to loch modan"}},{q="Who designed this tunnel?",a="It was designed by the master dwarven architect Franclorn Forgewright, the legendary artisan celebrated across Khaz Modan for designing the Stonewrought Dam and other monumental stone works.",al={"who built stonewrought pass","architect of pass","franclorn forgewright tunnel"}},{q="Why are the gates locked?",a="The gates are heavily barred on both sides to keep the fiery monsters and hostile Dark Iron dwarves of Searing Gorge from invading the inhabited lands of Loch Modan. Mountaineer Pebblebitty guards the Loch Modan entrance and requires authorization before granting passage.",al={"locked gate","why is pass locked","how to open gate"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="The tunnel stands as a testament to the engineering brilliance of Franclorn Forgewright, though it now abuts the grim, conquered territory of your wayward Dark Iron kin.",["faction:Alliance"]="Guarded by the dwarven Mountaineers, this locked passageway shields vulnerable settlements in Loch Modan from the volcanic threats festering in Searing Gorge."},kw={"dustfire valley","franclorn forgewright","loch modan","pebblebitty","searing gorge","stonewrought pass","valley of kings"},rel={"subzone:dustfire-valley","subzone:valley-of-kings","zone:searinggorge","zone:lochmodan","subzone:stonewrought-dam","topic:alliance"},src={"Stonewrought Pass"}}
E["subzone:thorium-point"] = {t="subzone",n="Thorium Point",z="searinggorge",s="Perched upon the northern bluffs of the Searing Gorge, Thorium Point serves as the primary staging camp for the Thorium Brotherhood. From this neutral outpost, these rogue Dark Iron dwarves recruit passing adventurers and strike back against their tyrannical kin deeper within the volcanic wastes.",h="Perched upon the northern bluffs of the Searing Gorge, Thorium Point serves as the primary staging camp for...",sec={{t="A Foothold Above the Ash",b="Overlooking the scorched slag heaps of the Searing Gorge, Thorium Point is a modest mountain encampment built out of necessity. It is held by the Thorium Brotherhood, a renegade faction of Dark Iron dwarves who have severed ties with their enslaved brethren in Shadowforge City. Unwilling to bow to the Firelord or Emperor Dagran Thaurissan, these outcasts maintain an open-air forge, a busy flight master, and a well-guarded perimeter northeast of Firewatch Ridge. Because of their desperate struggle for survival and master-level smithing aspirations, the Brotherhood keeps the camp open to both the Alliance and the Horde, welcoming anyone willing to dig ores out of the ash or bash Dark Iron skulls.",sp=0},{t="A Waystation for Wayfarers",b="Beyond being a staging ground for the Brotherhood's war against their brethren, Thorium Point is an indispensable crossroads in the heart of the Redridge mountain chain. Perched safely above the ravenous spiders and fire elementals that prowl the volcanic basin, the outpost offers direct flight links to Ironforge, as well as forward camps across the Badlands and the Burning Steppes. For wandering mercenaries, prospectors, and crafters looking to earn the secretive favor of master dwarf smiths, this smoky cliffside is the safest hearth to be found in the Gorge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Thorium Point?",a="The outpost is controlled by the Thorium Brotherhood, a group of breakaway Dark Iron dwarves who reject the rule of their fiery emperor and seek to forge their own destiny free from elemental servitude.",al={"who runs thorium point","thorium point owner","who lives at thorium point"}},{q="Why is Thorium Point neutral to both the Alliance and Horde?",a="The Thorium Brotherhood is vastly outnumbered by their hostile Dark Iron kin and the beasts of the Searing Gorge. They cannot afford to make enemies of traveling adventurers, so they trade freely and hire mercenaries regardless of faction allegiance.",al={"why can horde use thorium point","is thorium point neutral","alliance horde thorium point"}},{q="What services are available at Thorium Point?",a="The encampment features flight masters connecting to Ironforge, the Badlands and the Burning Steppes, alongside basic trade vendors, a working forge and anvil, and local work orders against the Dark Irons.",al={"flight path thorium point","what is at thorium point","thorium point vendors"}},{q="Where is Thorium Point located in Searing Gorge?",a="It is perched along the northern rock wall of Searing Gorge, situated high northeast of Firewatch Ridge overlooking the caldera floor.",al={"how to find thorium point","thorium point location","where is thorium point"}}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The Dark Iron smiths here hold trade secrets coveted by metalworkers across the world, offering rare plans to crafters who supply them with volcanic ore and components.",["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing Dark Iron dwarves who aren't immediately trying to murder you is rare, but Bronzebeard travelers know these outcasts are driven purely by craft and survival, not love for Ironforge."},kw={"blacksmithing","dark iron","firewatch ridge","flight path","searing gorge","thorium brotherhood","thorium point"},rel={"zone:searinggorge","subzone:firewatch-ridge","zone:burningsteppes","subzone:flame-crest","subzone:morgan-s-vigil","zone:ironforge","zone:badlands","subzone:kargath"},src={"Thorium Point"}}
E["zone:searinggorge"] = {t="zone",n="Searing Gorge",z="searinggorge",s="Searing Gorge is a scorched, desolate canyon in southern Khaz Modan, bordering Blackrock Mountain to the south. Once a verdant expanse of the Redridge Mountains, it was devastated over two centuries ago by the apocalyptic summoning of Ragnaros the Firelord. Today, the gorge is heavily worked by the Dark Iron clan, whose extensive slave mines in the Cauldron are closely monitored by the breakaway Thorium Brotherhood.",h="Searing Gorge is a scorched, desolate canyon in southern Khaz Modan, bordering Blackrock Mountain to the...",sec={{t="A Scorched Wasteland",b="Before the War of the Three Hammers, the territory that is now Searing Gorge was a green, rolling mountain region connected to the Redridge chain. That lush landscape ceased to exist over two hundred and thirty years ago when Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan, desperate to turn the tide of defeat, summoned Ragnaros from the depths beneath the world. The cataclysmic emergence of the Firelord tore the earth asunder, raised Blackrock Mountain, reduced the grand Dark Iron city of Thaurissan to smoking ruins, and burned the northern valley into a cracked expanse of ash, sulfur, and volcanic glass.",sp=0},{t="The Cauldron and the Slag Pit",b="Seeking raw materials to supply their war machine after the loss of their old capital, the Dark Iron dwarves seized the desolate gorge. In the center of the valley lies the Cauldron, a colossal open-pit excavation plunging deep into the stone. Within its lower recesses sits the Slag Pit, a brutal subterranean mining complex. Here, Dark Iron overseers and lumbering war golems drive captured enemies into grueling slave labor, pulling iron, mithril, and rare deposits of Dark Iron ore out of the burning rock under the constant threat of lava surges and roaming beasts.",sp=0},{t="Thorium Brotherhood and Contested Paths",b="Perched on the northern crags overlooking the excavation sits Thorium Point, the fortified outpost of the Thorium Brotherhood. Having split from their kin in Blackrock Mountain, these master craftsmen offer neutral shelter to travelers willing to undermine the Dark Iron operations or supply them with rare smelting components. Access to the gorge itself is tightly restricted: the Alliance keeps the Stonewrought Pass locked down behind heavy iron gates toward Loch Modan, while Horde expeditions from nearby Kargath have cut a narrow trail through the eastern badlands to scout the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Searing Gorge burned and covered in ash?",a="Over two hundred and thirty years ago, during the War of the Three Hammers, the Dark Iron Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan attempted to summon a supernatural power to avoid defeat. Instead, he summoned Ragnaros the Firelord. The cataclysmic eruption shattered the southern Redridge range, created the volcano of Blackrock Mountain, and incinerated the surrounding valleys into Searing Gorge and the Burning Steppes.",al={"why is it burnt","searing gorge lore","how was searing gorge created"}},{q="Who are the dwarves living at Thorium Point?",a="They belong to the Thorium Brotherhood, an independent faction of Dark Iron dwarves who severed ties with their imperial kin under Blackrock Mountain. From their camp atop Thorium Point, they work as master smiths and artificers, trading knowledge and crafting secrets to any traveler who aids them against the Dark Iron forces below.",al={"thorium point dwarves","who is thorium brotherhood","thorium brotherhood lore"}},{q="What is going on in the Cauldron?",a="The Cauldron is a massive open excavation dominated by the Dark Iron clan, containing the subterranean Slag Pit. Dark Iron overseers and war golems use captured prisoners as slave labor to extract precious ores—including valuable Dark Iron deposits—to feed the great forges inside Blackrock Mountain.",al={"what is the cauldron","the slag pit lore","what are dark irons mining"}},{q="How do you get into Searing Gorge from Loch Modan?",a="The passage from Loch Modan through Stonewrought Pass is barred by a heavy locked gate guarded by Ironforge mountaineers. Travelers must either obtain the Key to Searing Gorge through an official task for Curator Thorius, have a skilled rogue pick the mechanism, or bypass the gate entirely by taking the open trail south of Kargath in the Badlands.",al={"stonewrought pass gate","how to open searing gorge door","key to searing gorge"}},{q="Why is the Horde interested in Searing Gorge?",a="Operating from the nearby fortress of Kargath in the Badlands, Horde commanders carved a mountain pass into the gorge to scout Dark Iron troop movements and secure tactical routes toward Blackrock Mountain, which holds immense strategic importance.",al={"why is horde here","kargath gorge connection","horde presence"}},{q="Are there any dungeons or raid entrances inside Searing Gorge?",a="There are no instance portals directly in the gorge itself, but the southern entrance leads straight into Blackrock Mountain. That mountain houses Blackrock Depths, Blackrock Spire, and the deep passages leading into the Molten Core.",al={"searing gorge instances","dungeons in searing gorge","where is molten core"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves of Ironforge, Searing Gorge is a bitter reminder of the War of the Three Hammers and the catastrophic folly of the Dark Iron clan, whose excavations now threaten Khaz Modan's southern approaches.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance keeps the gate at Stonewrought Pass locked to isolate the Dark Irons from peaceful dwarven settlements in Loch Modan, though courageous adventurers are sanctioned to strike into the gorge.",["faction:Horde"]="Using Kargath as a staging base, the Horde cut an overland approach into the gorge to gather intelligence on Blackrock Mountain and disrupt Dark Iron operations in Khaz Modan.",["profession:Mining"]="The volcanic landscape and deep excavations in the Slag Pit make Searing Gorge one of the primary hunting grounds for rich veins of mithril, truesilver, and coveted Dark Iron ore.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues with seasoned lockpicking skill are valued travelers here, as they can bypass the locked Stonewrought Pass gate connecting Loch Modan directly to the gorge."},kw={"blackrock mountain","cauldron","dark iron clan","ragnaros","searing gorge","slag pit","stonewrought pass","thorium brotherhood","thorium point"},rel={"subzone:blackrock-mountain","subzone:thorium-point","subzone:cauldron","subzone:slag-pit","subzone:stonewrought-pass","zone:badlands","zone:burningsteppes","topic:dark-iron-clan"},src={"Searing Gorge (Classic)","Searing Gorge"}}
